---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import Header from '../components/Header.astro';
import Footer from '../components/Footer.astro';

const description = 'Why decant-core is AGPL-3.0, and what that means for your project.';
---

<BaseLayout title="License — decant-core" description={description} canonicalPath="/license.html">
  <Header />
  <main class="page-section shell">
    <span class="eyebrow">License</span>
    <h1>
      The AGPL Open Commons <span style="color: var(--wine)">manifesto</span>.
    </h1>
    <p class="lede">
      <code>decant-core</code> is licensed under the{' '}
      <strong>GNU Affero General Public License v3.0 (AGPL-3.0-only)</strong>. That choice is not
      incidental — it is a product decision.
    </p>

    <h2>Parser infrastructure belongs in a shared commons</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      AI platforms change constantly. Every time ChatGPT redecorates a message or Claude changes how
      artifacts render, somebody has to re-learn the DOM. If each exporter maintains its own private
      parser stack, a platform update means the same broken logic gets re-debugged dozens of times —
      and the fixes disappear forever.
    </p>
    <p class="lede">
      decant-core exists to be the opposite: a shared copyleft commons where improvements stay
      available to the ecosystem instead of being siloed into proprietary forks.
    </p>

    <h2>What AGPL means for you</h2>
    <ul style="padding-left: 20px; color: var(--muted)">
      <li>
        <strong>Open-source projects (FOSS Exception)</strong> — You are welcome to link, import, or
        bundle decant-core into any project distributed under an OSI-approved open source license
        (such as MPL-2.0, MIT, Apache-2.0, or BSD) without requiring your project to adopt AGPLv3.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Running a modified version as a network service</strong> — If your modified version
        supports remote interaction through a computer network, you must prominently offer all users
        interacting with it remotely an opportunity to receive the Corresponding Source of your
        modified version at no charge. This is the clause that keeps parser fixes available to the
        commons even behind a server.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Proprietary, closed-source, or commercial use</strong> — If your product cannot
        comply with AGPLv3, commercial licenses are available. Contact{' '}
        <a href="mailto:office@covai.org">office@covai.org</a> for licensing terms.
      </li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Where to see the full terms</h2>
    <p class="lede">
      The complete text lives in{' '}
      <a href="https://github.com/Covai-Labs/decant/blob/main/LICENSE">LICENSE</a>. Our natural
      community is open-source extensions, exporters, archival and research tools, and self-hosted
      applications — projects that can contribute fixes back to the commons.
    </p>
  </main>
  <Footer />
</BaseLayout>
